WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Emira IV sits alongside in Gossport, UK, as of 5th October with only one recorded outing since arriving on 4th September. This is Offshore North, Episode 8. Every 4 years, a small number of sailors set out alone on the hardest race in the sport, and one Canadian is trying to become the first to finish it. On the Canadian boat, as of 5th October, the team's YB tracker shows Emira IV alongside in Gossport, UK, in Port Smith Harbor. The tracker records just one outing in the 30-day window since the boat arrived.

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:35.460
arrived on 4th September. That was a training run on 17th September that reached 76 kilometers

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:40.340
south of the Isle of White before returning to the birth shortly after midnight. The boat

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:45.760
reached the Gossport birth at 9pm UTC on 4th September after the delivery from Canada.

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:50.860
No other movements show up in the trackers' 30-day window. The campaign's own channels

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:55.820
carried no new posts in the past seven days. The most recent Scott's notes entry is still

00:00:55.820 --> 00:00:58.640
the second September reflection on the summer in Cullingwood.

00:00:59.060 --> 00:01:02.820
In that post, Shire described learning the boat's systems one by one.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:08.420
Sales, rigging, foils, electrical, hydro generators, solar and autopilot overlays.

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:13.500
He noted that he has sailed Lake Huron for more than 40 years, so the water itself held

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:16.820
few surprises, while the boat's complexity was the real learning.

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:21.820
On two heavy days, his triceps seized on the grinder, which he traced to pushing rather

00:01:21.820 --> 00:01:26.240
them pulling because of a shoulder injury and to not drinking enough water with electrolytes.

00:01:26.660 --> 00:01:32.160
He wrote that he has not yet sailed Emira IV in open ocean waves and swell and that he

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:33.160
needs to remain humble.

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:37.880
The support team named in the post includes Martin Amesqua, who has been with the boat

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:44.300
for a long time, Gabi Bucal, Clovis Gautier, Julina Bayat for rigging in systems, Alberto

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:49.320
Zacharia for electrical, computer and sensor systems, Alan Roberts for coaching on the

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:54.900
excess set rooting system and autopilot overlays and Nick Maloney as sailing coach. The position

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:59.920
and the single dated outing are therefore the only fresh facts available this week. They confirmed

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:04.240
the boat has completed the transatlantic delivery and is now based in the UK rather than

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:09.060
Brittany, with preparation for the route to rum proceeding from Gossport. Shire remains

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:14.060
outside the official entry list for that race as of 4 October, so the stated goal stays

00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:20.540
aiming to start on 1 November. The 2 September post also records that Imira IV was leaving Canada

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:25.740
and heading back to Europe at that time, consistent with the tractor-fix at Cosport 4 days later.

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:31.700
Now, the fleet. Tural team has been cut in half at the waterline, so the scour-shaped hull

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:36.720
bottom can be replaced with a new-shaped design to let the boat fly flatter and longer on its

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:42.580
foils. The work, the first of its kind on an IMOCA, began after the boats returned from the

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:47.780
transat cafe lower victory and is scheduled to finish in June, leaving six months before

00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:48.560
the root do-rum.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:53.660
The change trades a small loss of power for reduced hydrodynamic drag once the boat is

00:02:53.660 --> 00:02:54.360
fully airborne.

00:02:55.240 --> 00:03:00.200
Jeremy Bayou explained that when the boat flew flat, the original scow-haul was not optimal.

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:05.380
Nicholas and Drio added that the heel was lower than expected, prompting the new hull

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:05.620
shape.

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:11.000
The two new hull haves were fabricated over the past year by Jepetto Composite, a few

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:16.240
meters from Charles Hanger. The structural work is being done with GERIT, the same company

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:23.240
that built the original structure. VPLP collaborated on the design since winter 2024. The goal is

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:27.820
to improve foiling phases, enhance performance on certain points of sale, and make the

00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:34.100
boat easier to handle solo. A permanent 1,674 square meter race control building is under

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:40.520
construction at Port Olona in La Sabla, Dolaun, at a cost of 8.8 million euros. The facility,

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:46.280
due for delivery in June 2028, will replace temporary structures used only during the Vende Globe,

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:51.740
and will serve year-round for other offshore events, including the Vende Arctic and New York Vende.

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:58.120
The building permit was signed on September 16, 2026. Demolition of existing buildings is scheduled

00:03:58.120 --> 00:04:04.740
to begin in January 2027. The project is carried by Vende expansion, and the building will also host

00:04:04.740 --> 00:04:09.940
seminars and professional events outside race periods. The question of utilization rate between

00:04:09.940 --> 00:04:14.660
additions remains open, and the programming of events and activities is intended to keep the

00:04:14.660 --> 00:04:21.220
site active year-round. Baptiste Hulin, 29, will line up on 1st November for his first root-to-rum

00:04:21.220 --> 00:04:24.500
one in the Ocean 50 class aboard Biabolus Oceons.

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:30.980
He won the 2025 Transact Cafe Lore and says the result gave the team legitimacy in a class

00:04:30.980 --> 00:04:34.940
where the top four boats finished within 45 minutes of one another last year.

00:04:35.560 --> 00:04:39.880
Hulin is aiming to win more major races in the tightly matched 50-foot trim ran fleet.

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:46.720
He arrived in the Biabolus Oceons project in 2024 after Pierre Kiroga and spent a year

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:50.160
sailing with Thomas Rooksell, who remains part of his routing team.

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:54.640
Whulin described the victory as showing the team they were capable of winning and giving

00:04:54.640 --> 00:04:59.120
the whole project more energy, while remaining humble because the top four were so close.

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:04.580
He has made St. Molo his home and is one of 11 sailors entered in the Ocean 50 for the

00:05:04.580 --> 00:05:05.600
solo transatlantic.

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:07.180
Time for plane sailing.

00:05:07.820 --> 00:05:12.880
An Imoka 60s foils do not simply reduce drag, they lift the entire hull clear of the water

00:05:12.880 --> 00:05:14.300
once boat speed is high enough.

00:05:14.820 --> 00:05:18.880
When that happens, the wedded surface drops dramatically, and the boat can sustain speeds

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:24.100
above 30 knots for long periods. The trade-off is that the boat must be kept relatively flat

00:05:24.100 --> 00:05:28.900
so the foils stay at the correct angle. Too much heel and the leeward foil loses lift

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:34.260
while the windward one comes out of the water. Modern designs therefore adjust foil angle and hull

00:05:34.260 --> 00:05:39.520
shape together, which is exactly what the shirol refit is testing. The result is a boat that spends

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:44.720
more time flying and less time pushing a heavy hull through waves. The new hull on shirol 2

00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:49.540
is intended to improve glide while accepting a slight mechanical loss of power from reduced

00:05:49.540 --> 00:05:54.500
heel, with the net gain coming from lower hydrodynamic drag once the boat is airborne.

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:59.960
This kind of optimization is constant in the class because small changes in how long a boat stays

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:06.720
foiling can add up over thousands of miles. And the countdown. 769 days remain until the

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:12.520
Von Day Globe start on November 12, 2028. The next concrete milestone for the Canadian campaign

00:06:12.520 --> 00:06:18.060
is the opening of the Root-Duram race village in St. Mallow in 15 days, and that's the

00:06:18.060 --> 00:06:19.160
week in offshore racing.

